---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Getting started" description="Install and use @navigato/react">
  <h1>Getting started</h1>

  <p class="nvg-lead">
    <code>@navigato/react</code> is <strong>0.2.0</strong> in this repo. It is
    <strong>not on the public npm registry</strong>. Public booking parts are
    <code>preview</code>, not <code>stable</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Status</h2>
  <p>
    Peer React is <code>&gt;=18</code> (<code>react</code> / <code>react-dom</code>).
    Package exports: <code>.</code>, <code>./styles.css</code> (built
    <code>dist/navigato.css</code>), and <code>./theme.css</code> (copied
    <code>dist/theme.css</code> from <code>src/styles/global.css</code>). See the repo
    <a href="https://github.com/andreortiz82/nvgto-styleguide/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md">CHANGELOG</a>
    for the SERP / PDP floor and remaining booking docs. Do not expect
    <code>npm install @navigato/react</code> to resolve until Andre publishes.
  </p>

  <h2>Consume today</h2>
  <p>
    Clone the monorepo and import from the workspace, or copy
    <code>packages/navigato/src</code> when you must edit files. Override tokens
    before forking.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`git clone https://github.com/andreortiz82/nvgto-styleguide.git
cd nvgto-styleguide
npm install`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Import styles &amp; fonts</h2>
  <p>Add the Navigato stylesheet (and optionally the theme file) in your app entry:</p>
  <pre><code>{`import '@navigato/react/styles.css'
// optional tokens-only path:
// import '@navigato/react/theme.css'`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    In your HTML head (or root layout) — the package does not inject fonts. Cinzel and Jost are
    SIL OFL Google Fonts. Neue Haas and Futura are commercial; do not vendor them. Navigato UI
    uses the Helvetica Neue system stack.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cinzel:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Jost:ital,wght@0,300;0,400;0,500;0,600;0,700;1,400&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    Set the brand on <code>html</code>. Dark is still the <code>.dark</code> class.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`<html data-brand="navigato">
<!-- or data-brand="nox-vale" -->
<!-- class="dark" for dark mode -->
</html>`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Use components</h2>
  <p>
    0.2.0 ships shadcn/ui primitives plus booking composites. Booking entries in
    the registry that set <code>status: "preview"</code> render the DESIGN.md
    skeleton (when / when-not, anatomy, states, a11y, do/don’t, typed props).
    Atoms stay thin.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`import {
  BookingSearchBar,
  ListingCard,
  BookingWidget,
} from '@navigato/react'

export function SearchPage() {
  return (
    <div className="navigato-root">
      <BookingSearchBar />
      <ListingCard
        title="Navigato Loft"
        location="South Congress, Austin"
        pricePerNight={189}
        rating={4.9}
        reviewCount={128}
        imageUrl="/hotel.jpg"
      />
      <BookingWidget pricePerNight={220} />
    </div>
  )
}`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Root wrapper</h2>
  <p>
    Wrap your app (or Storybook) in <code>.navigato-root</code> to apply base typography:
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`<div className="navigato-root">{children}</div>`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Publish later</h2>
  <p>
    When the package goes to npm (Andre), the install becomes
    <code>npm install @navigato/react</code>. Until then, do not treat that
    snippet as live. Publish path (do not run from a docs PR):
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`npm run build:lib
npm publish --workspace=@navigato/react`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    <code>publishConfig.access</code> is <code>public</code>. Do not bump to 1.0
    while booking parts are <code>preview</code>. 0.x may break; prefer a
    deprecation first.
  </p>

  <h2>shadcn/ui foundation</h2>
  <p>
    Primitives live under <code>components/ui/</code> in the package source. To add more shadcn
    components, run the CLI from <code>packages/navigato</code> — see
    <a href="https://ui.shadcn.com/">shadcn/ui docs</a>. Restyle via tokens. Do not fork Button
    or Dialog because the brand changed. Set <code>data-brand</code> and tokens instead.
  </p>

  <h2>Accessibility</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}getting-started/accessibility/`}>Accessibility guidelines →</a>
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
